R2826 evidence - the value-domain assertion is now SAID OUT LOUD
criterion AC-VD9: one 'value-domain:' line per face, parsed from
that face's own stdout; AC-VD10: the literal lives only in
tools/value_domain.py; AC-VD11: the formatter refuses PASS over an
empty comparison and each face folds the same reason into its own
failure list, so the printed line and the exit code cannot disagree.

payment_gate_report          rc=0 lines=1
    value-domain: PASS products=5 tiers=0
money_path_demo              rc=0 lines=1
    value-domain: PASS products=5 tiers=0
membership_face              rc=0 lines=1
    value-domain: PASS products=5 tiers=1
membership_benefit_report    rc=0 lines=1
    value-domain: PASS products=0 tiers=4

formatter negative control (AC-VD11):
    line(0, 0, [])          -> value-domain: FAIL 1 (products=0 tiers=0) E_VALUE_DOMAIN no row was compared against the catalog, so the formatter refuses to print PASS
    line(2, 0, [])          -> value-domain: PASS products=2 tiers=0
    line(0, 2, [])          -> value-domain: PASS products=0 tiers=2
    line(1, 0, ['E_VALUE_DOMAIN x']) -> value-domain: FAIL 1 (products=1 tiers=0) E_VALUE_DOMAIN x

the regression this window found while verifying (disclosed, fixed):
    three adjacent suites (payment_gate_report / money_path_demo /
    membership_face) imported the face tools by path with no tools/ on
    sys.path, so the R2825 sibling import died with ModuleNotFoundError
    and test_payment_gate_report was additionally red on its own import
    allowlist; both were repaired at their birth sites and the three
    suites plus this one now read PASS 13/13, 18/18 and 28/28.
    money_path_demo's AC-MPD6 then caught a REAL defect of the R2825
    wiring: faces called VD.catalog(ROOT), and the suite repoints ROOT
    at a temp world, so the catalog read empty and every product read
    'not in the catalog'. The catalog root is now derived from the
    tool's own path (CATALOG_ROOT) and cannot be repointed.
